{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"7d10ede9812d057bd56dc044da79fd6a3d441ef825b8d7583732dfb51569db57","packTokens":2452,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":208,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":666,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1472,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using authorized Folio3 Google accounts and have employee and vehicle profiles populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking and schedule releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can receive notifications and claim available spaces first-come, first-served.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record verification attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and automatically email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What should each role be able to view and do, especially security guards handling verification and administrators handling employee-level reports?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Employees see their own records; guards see the information needed to verify entry; administrators manage records and see configured reports.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"If a temporary claimant has multiple registered vehicles, which plate or plates should the entrance check accept for that employee's claim?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Accept any vehicle plate registered to the claimant for the claimed date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"When claim requests arrive at nearly the same time for the last available space, how should the system determine which request is first?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The first request accepted by the service gets the space; later requests fail and see refreshed availability.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What evidence should count as an actual vehicle entry for utilization reporting, rather than merely a camera detection or authorization attempt?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have security record whether the vehicle actually entered after the check.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should existing employee, dedicated-space, floor, and registered-vehicle records be loaded for launch?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Parking administrators enter the initial records in the app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Can a temporary parking user cancel a successfully allocated claim, and what happens to that space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"An employee may cancel at any time, and the space becomes available immediately.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should security guards and parking administrators authenticate, given that Google sign-in is specified for employees but not for these roles?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require Folio3 Google accounts for guards and administrators as well.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Who selects and maintains the stakeholders who receive the weekly utilization email?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Parking administrators manage the report recipient list in the app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict sign-in to authorized Folio3 Google Workspace accounts for employees, security guards, and parking administrators; reject personal Gmail and other provider accounts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Identify employees by corporate email, retrieve their employee ID and name from the corporate directory, and associate those fields with app-maintained dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle profiles; preserve the plate captured on existing claims when profile plates change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Require non-dedicated employees with no registered plate to save at least one plate before accessing the dashboard; make vehicle make, model, and color optional, and direct incomplete returning profiles to registration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Deny application access when Google authentication succeeds but the employee profile cannot be identified or retrieved from the corporate directory, returning a retryable error and contact path.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict employees to their own records, limit guards to information needed for entry verification, and allow administrators to manage records and access configured reports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Allow administrators to enter and maintain parking-space inventory, assigned floors, dedicated holders, employee parking assignments, and registered vehicles, including initial launch records; apply plate changes to future dates while retaining recorded plates on existing claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let only dedicated parking holders release today's parking through a single home-screen action, prevent duplicate releases for the same holder and date, and show Reserved, Released, or Claimed status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Let dedicated holders schedule releases for one or more future dates up to 30 calendar days ahead and persist each selected release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Use a configurable Daily Parking Release Time defaulting to 08:00 office-local time; make scheduled releases and same-day releases created before that time claimable at that time, and same-day releases created at or after it claimable immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Publish the current available-space count and send push notifications to eligible employees without dedicated parking whenever one or more spaces become claimable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee request accepted by the service, limit each employee to one temporary claim per date, and return refreshed availability to later unsuccessful claimants.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Assign a successful claimant one available space and its floor, record the claim date, time, employee, and assigned space for audit, and do not require proof that the employee parked on the assigned floor.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Allow employees to cancel successful temporary claims at any time and make the claimed space available immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Process license-plate-recognition detections for cars, ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects, and bypass temporary system verification for vehicles marked with a permanent parking sticker.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"For a readable plate on an unstickered vehicle, verify it against a temporary claim for the current office-local date using any plate registered to the claimant for the claimed date, and activate the green indicator only for valid authorization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"If a plate is unreadable or unverifiable, or the camera, authorization service, or indicator is unavailable, make no automated authorization, issue no green-indicator activation, and record an unreadable, unverifiable, or outage event.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Record every temporary verification attempt with its date, time, detected plate or unreadable status, and verification result, and let security record whether the vehicle actually entered after the check.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Use recorded actual-entry outcomes, rather than camera detections or authorization attempts alone, to preserve utilization history and identify dedicated parking that was not released and had no entry, and temporary claims that had no entry.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Generate and email a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office-local timezone to configured stakeholders, covering the preceding complete Monday-to-Sunday week and containing unused dedicated and temporary parking employees, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and temporary-claim totals, and an overall utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Let administrators add, update, and remove the stakeholder list used for weekly report emails in the app, accepting only addresses already authorized as report stakeholders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Provision the first parking administrator from a deployment-configured Folio3 account and let administrators assign employee, security-guard, and administrator roles to other authorized Folio3 accounts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}